1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,113
Where does most ATP come from?

2
00:00:02,363 --> 00:00:04,966
Not glycolysis, and not the Krebs cycle.

3
00:00:05,416 --> 00:00:09,512
It's the electron transport chain, on the inner mitochondrial membrane.

4
00:00:09,762 --> 00:00:15,074
H+ flows back through ATP synthase, which makes most of the ATP.

5
00:00:15,524 --> 00:00:19,449
And the final electron acceptor at the end of that chain is oxygen.

6
00:00:19,899 --> 00:00:22,651
These came from notes, each linked to its source line.

7
00:00:22,901 --> 00:00:26,379
Paste in your own lecture notes and check every card against them.
